{
 "kind": "mode_anchors",
 "_comment": "One anchor per (domain x mode) cell, 70 in total. The domain axis says WHAT IS ACTED ON -- HEAL=condition, CONSTRUCT=structure, FABRICATE=output, BOND=relation, STUDY=knowledge -- and the mode axis says WHAT ACT. Hints are mode-pure and domain-pure and deliberately span three registers (human, machine, organisational): the classifier embeds name+hints and nothing else, so a cell that only speaks one register cannot attract the others' records. Rewritten for Gate 0 after a 2026-09-07 audit found 43.3% of a deterministic sample filed in a cell its own anchor did not describe -- largely because every domain was anchored in one register (HEAL=Body, CONSTRUCT=Build, FABRICATE=Make, BOND=Connect, STUDY=Mind). Full contract: docs/GRID_AXES.md.",
